{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1375461-what-to-pack-for-an-umbral-excursion","id":1375461,"title":"What to Pack for an Umbral Excursion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-18T11:50:20-07:00","id":1375461,"title":"What to Pack for an Umbral Excursion?","content":"The year is 1938. Master Dusty Abrams is the leader of the Dustguard cabal in the Oklahoma Panhandle. Up until recently, he was in the Order of Hermes House Luxor, now he belongs to the Society of Ether. The local Penumbra is crawling with drought-spirits. When the big dust storms rage, the Gauntlet is often torn and malicious spirits cross over. His cabal consists of John Cloudwalker (Dreamspeakers), Harpoon Harriet (Society of Ether), Samuel \u201cPreacher\u201d Hansen (Celestial Chorus), and Moses \u201cThe Kid\u201d Freeman (Euthanatos). They have devoted themselves to protecting the Midwest from these spirits.<br /> <br /> My group will likely come to the Panhandle looking for help to get to Horizon via a Hidden Way, which of course will set the stage for an Umbral adventure. So, what kind of equipment do you think Ol' Dusty would deem to be essential for a cabal journeying into the Velvet Shadow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T12:22:33-07:00","id":1375465,"title":"","content":"Several changes of underwear seems prudent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;</span>Explanations exist; they have existed for all time; there is always a well-known solution to every human problem \u2014 neat, plausible, and wrong.<span style=\"font-size:14px\">&quot;<br /> - H.L. Mencken</span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/467-bob-the-skull","name":"Bob the Skull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar467_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T12:36:35-07:00","id":1375468,"title":"","content":"Food and water. Spirits are tricky to eat, and it saves food summoners to have to waste energy on food.<br /> <br /> Tass. It's generally useful and Spirits sometimes will trade favors for it.<br /> <br /> A spirit ally or two.<br /> <br /> Amulets or other rituals to protect the travelers against known dangers (as defined by the ST) could be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T14:20:36-07:00","id":1375483,"title":"","content":"Carrying around as much water and somewhat significant knock knacks could also be a good idea. You never know what the local spirits might be willing to trade for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T12:55:15-07:00","id":1375673,"title":"","content":"Dusty's Umbral Adventure Packing List:<br /> <br /> Clean underwear <br /> Knitted sweater<br /> Thermos bottle of coffee <br /> Eight PB &amp; J sandwiches <br /> Spam and beans (10 lbs.)<br /> Ground coffee beans<br /> Gallon of water <br /> Camp stove<br /> Sleeping bag<br /> 100' string<br /> Matches<br /> Flashlight <br /> Notebook and pencil <br /> <br /> For barter and trade:<br /> No less than 10 drams of tass<br /> Gold rings and jewelry, at least half a dozen pieces<br /> Postcards, at least half a dozen<br /> A pint of whisky.<br /> Tobacco<br /> Chocolate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T00:17:16-07:00","id":1375766,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0iRTB-FTMdk\" target=\"_blank\">Fighting trousers</a> of course! (The time travel trousers might also be a good second choice). Good for gaining respect in those duels in umbrood courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Di